From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Turcios <turcioskevinr@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 23:30:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Optimization: Avoid importing "inspect" and "typing" at
 startup

Every compiled program imported "inspect" at startup, only to patch it
for compiled generators and coroutines, and with 3.12 or higher also
"typing", only to reach "TypeVar", "ParamSpec", and "TypeVarTuple". That
cost about half the startup time of a small program.

In standalone mode, the loader sees every module being imported, so
"inspect" and "types" are now patched right after they are first
loaded, next to the post load code of plugins, or immediately if they
are loaded already. Other modes keep importing them at startup, as the
loader may not see them imported there. The typing types are taken from
the built-in "_typing" module that defines them.

A standalone "hello world" on macOS with Python 3.14 goes from 17.5ms
to 9.1ms.

Co-authored-by: wtfyd-agent[bot] <328989958+wtfyd-agent[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Signed-off-by: Kevin Turcios <turcioskevinr@gmail.com>
